{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>לשובע</b> Four times in the Masorah. Here, and another in the portion of Behar, and another in our [reading of] Shabbat — regarding the pot of meat — \"eating bread to satiety,\" and another: \"He sent them provisions לשובע.\" In all of them, שובע is mentioned in connection with bread or fruit, because it is written in the context of settled habitation. But when they were in the wilderness: \"He sent them provisions לשובע\" — for He needed to provide all their provisions לשובע." "<b>לשובע</b> in gematria: אפילו אוכל קימעא (even if one eats a little)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The phrase סיר הבשר (pot of meat) likely alludes to Numbers 11:8 (manna prepared in pots); the third occurrence's context and the reading of 'בשבתנו' are uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:41.866796350Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}